    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d121">

                <pb facs="0145" n="131" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg131"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.933/7–844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-19T19:00:00-04:00">July 19, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>984. The detail of four officers for special duty with the Army was at the
                    request of War Department to State, your 1182, July 8, 1 p.m. Requests for
                    similar detail of other officers should come through same channel. This
                    Department holds that such details having been approved, it is for the
                    Ambassador and ranking Army officer to work out details, substitutions,
                    transfers, et cetera, by mutual agreement and normally the Department would
                    follow Ambassador’s recommendations. Appropriateness of Service’s inclusion in
                    group going to communist areas and his status there is case in point.</p>
                <p>Department believes Foreign Service officers can render constructive service to
                    Army, but only if their status as members of your staff detailed to military
                    organizations is clearly recognized and closest liaison maintained between Army
                    headquarters and Embassy.</p>
                <p>Foregoing has been repeated to Mission at New Delhi which has been directed to
                    instruct Davies that he should communicate Department’s <pb facs="0146" n="132"
                        xml:id="pg132"/> views to senior Army officer at General Stilwell’s
                    Headquarters, New Delhi, and that Davies should strictly observe procedure set
                    forth above in connection with any personnel matters of this nature.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
